~ beginning
Hericlitus: No man steps in the same river twice, for it is not the same river and he is not the same man
=> END

~ narration
This is the limbo, the space between life and death. 

To move on to the afterlife, you must build your boat using your life’s memories. 

Each stage of the journey, you will be offered 3 memories to choose from to build your boat, which may contribute to the style, sturdiness, and size of your boat.

You start on a mini raft, here is a series of choices (tutorial); [#reveal]
- First one
	You picked the first one.
- Second one
	You picked the second one.
- Start again => narration
- End tutorial => game

~ game
Welcome to your journey! The afterlife demands that you build a boat as you make your way to your desired afterlife. The great beyond’s magic will grant you whatever you desire to reach it. Here is how it’ll work;

Sample card () - Here, you are given a situation, then you make your choice
Decorate your boat +10 style
Add more material +10 sturdiness
Make it bigger!! _+10 size

There will, however, be sacrifices most of the time. Of course, everything comes with a price;
Make it even bigger! +6 size  -5 sturdiness
Strengthen the material +6 sturdiness -5 style
Carve drawings into your raft +6 style -5 size

There will, however, be sacrifices most of the time. Of course, everything comes with a price;
 - Make it even bigger! +6 size  -5 sturdiness
 - Strengthen the material +6 sturdiness -5 style
 - Carve drawings into your raft +6 style -5 size

Some sacrifices are much bigger than others. As you inch closer to a peaceful oblivion, you may have to sacrifice your memories. 
> Some of your supplies go overboard, what do you do?
 - Use all your supplies, losing everything you need for the journey ahead. -20 style, sturdiness, size
 - Lay one of your memories to rest, refilling your supplies, even if you have to let it go forever.

As you go along your journey, dear player, reflect on what it means to give all that you know up. 

You want to relax, easing into your journey, what do you decide to do?
 - Watch the stars, noting the beautiful colours  + 7 style
 - Lean over the edge and run your hand through the water  + 7 sturdiness
 - Take a nap, enjoying the breeze + 7 size

You check your supplies, seeing what you can do to keep you busy. 
 - Illuminate your walls with your star lights +6 styles - 4 sturdiness
 - Make your boat more homey and comfortable + 7 sturdiness -6 size
 - Build a makeshift lamp + 7 size -3 style

You decide to go fishing for stars,  what do you do?
 - Build a makeshift fishing rod  + 5 sturdiness -3 size
 - Reach into the water, hoping to catch one in your hand + 2 size -1 style
 - Look for the one that shines the brightest, then try to swipe it as you pass by it + 5 style -4 sturdiness.

As you lie in bed, exhaustion hits you (yes, you still can still feel exhausted in death). The stars out on the river still shine bright, how do you solve this to achieve a peaceful rest?
 - Fashion a nice blanket out of your materials + 5 style - 2 size
 - Build a small shelter, angled so that minimal light reaches your eyes +6 size  -2 style
 - Do nothing, the light is calming and warm + 4 sturdiness -3 size


=> END
